Got it—no Audacity.” He paused, eyes flicking to her notebook. “What’s the crowd?”  

“Mr. Kowalski’s cousins, plus three skeptics who think barbershop is elevator music. I need a hook that slaps.”  

“Drop the ‘shoo-fly’ rhythm into the second verse—fast enough to wake up the room, slow enough to keep the pitch. Pair it with a harmony that keeps the vowels round;

Noted: twin wheels, screw-in axles, matte finish. Pro tip—put a rubber band around each zipper pull; stops them from snagging and keeps the shell from cracking when you shove it into tight overhead bins."

Sabine zipped the main compartment, then the front pocket, feeling the tension line hold. "How about the handle? Breaks at the base on my old one."

